From 87a5149d1364b5f3dc9c773c8114d97f13bc01e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:21:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0301 -- format guard on drawTileFast

`_blit_indexed` assumes INDEX8 on both sides and moves one byte per
pixel. `drawTileFast` called it with no format check at all.

The sibling `drawTileFastToSurface` states the assumption in its own
comment and falls back to SDL_BlitSurface when either side disagrees.
`drawTileFast` never got that fallback, and nothing upstream supplies
one: map.cpp gates the call on `drawtile_fast_on`, which resolves through
`drawtile_fast_active()` to `_abl_drawtile_fast()` -- a bare
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DRAWTILE_FAST env read, default ON, with no
indexed-mode or format condition anywhere in the chain.

So against an RGB565 window surface the entire tilemap layer wrote one
byte per pixel into a two-byte-per-pixel destination. Half the bytes, at
the wrong addresses. The visible result is a corrupted tilemap; the
invisible one is that the frame also gets cheaper, because it is doing
half the writes it should.

REACHABLE WITHOUT A KILLSWITCH, which is what makes this a user-facing
bug rather than a diagnostic curiosity. initVideo sets `_indexed_mode =
false` and logs "FALLBACK to RGB565" whenever `master.pal` or
`master.map` fails to load -- missing file, short read, or the 8.3-alias
probe failing on an LFN-less filesystem. Those files are generated
per-user by tools/build-master-palette.py against their own extracted
Cave Story data, so a user who skips or botches that step lands in RGB565
and gets a corrupted tilemap. And unlike the paths 0297 touched, this
site has no dimension gate either, so it happens on EVERY card, not only
one whose smallest VBE mode exceeds the logical screen.

Found while auditing the 16bpp probe cell from round 2, where it
contaminated the measurement: that run was reported as ~3x faster than
its 8bpp counterpart while also showing "lots of new corruption", and one
mechanism produced both. The performance conclusion drawn from that cell
was withdrawn; the bug it exposed is this.

The fix mirrors the sibling exactly: dispatch to `_blit_indexed` only
when both surfaces are INDEX8, otherwise SDL_BlitSurface, which handles
arbitrary formats and honours the source colorkey set at load time. The
rects handed to either path are the post-clip, post-translate ones, so
patch 0296's centring still applies on the fallback.

`src_sfc` and the destination are hoisted into locals and null-checked
first. That is not defensive padding: the fallback dereferences both
through SDL_BlitSurface, so the guard is a precondition of introducing
it, not an unrelated hardening.

Trade accepted: on the RGB565 path this is slower than what it replaced.
What it replaced was fast and wrong. RGB565 is a degraded fallback
configuration whose users currently see a broken screen, so correctness
wins without argument. The INDEX8 path -- every normally configured
install, and every cell in the banked benchmark matrix -- is untouched
apart from two pointer compares that fold away against the blit.

No new banner: this adds a guard and an error log that fires only on
SDL_BlitSurface failure, not a lever with a boot-time witness.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/graphics/Renderer.cpp | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
index 7f1655f0..19733e26 100644
--- a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
@@ -7867,10 +7867,49 @@ void Renderer::drawTileFast(Surface *src, int dstx, int dsty, int srcx, int srcy
   // path eventually reaches via _try_fast_blit dispatch). Wave-25
   // instrumentation continues to fire if g_mds_tfg_loop_active is
   // set by the caller.
-  _blit_indexed(_cached_window_surface, src->surfaceCpu(),
-                srcrect, dstrect,
-                (Uint8)src->colorkey(), src->hasColorkey(),
-                src->spanTable());
+  //
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0301): format guard. `_blit_indexed` assumes
+  // INDEX8<->INDEX8 and moves ONE byte per pixel; the sibling
+  // `drawTileFastToSurface` says so in as many words and falls back to
+  // SDL_BlitSurface when either side disagrees. This function never got
+  // that fallback, and nothing upstream supplies one -- `map.cpp` gates
+  // the call on `drawtile_fast_on`, which resolves to a bare
+  // SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DRAWTILE_FAST env read with no format condition at
+  // all. So against an RGB565 window surface the whole tilemap layer wrote
+  // one byte per pixel into a two-byte-per-pixel destination: half the
+  // bytes, at the wrong addresses, which is corruption that also happens
+  // to look faster.
+  //
+  // Reachable WITHOUT any killswitch. `initVideo` sets `_indexed_mode =
+  // false` and logs "FALLBACK to RGB565" whenever `master.pal` or
+  // `master.map` fails to load -- a missing file, a short read, or the 8.3
+  // alias probe failing. A user in that state gets a corrupted tilemap on
+  // EVERY card, not only oversized ones, because this site has no
+  // dimension gate either.
+  SDL_Surface *const _tf_dst = _cached_window_surface;
+  SDL_Surface *const _tf_src = src ? src->surfaceCpu() : nullptr;
+  if (!_tf_dst || !_tf_src) return;
+
+  if (_tf_src->format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_INDEX8 &&
+      _tf_dst->format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_INDEX8)
+  {
+    _blit_indexed(_tf_dst, _tf_src,
+                  srcrect, dstrect,
+                  (Uint8)src->colorkey(), src->hasColorkey(),
+                  src->spanTable());
+  }
+  else
+  {
+    // Same fallback as drawTileFastToSurface: SDL_BlitSurface handles
+    // arbitrary formats and honours the source colorkey set at load. The
+    // rects handed over are the post-clip, post-translate ones, so the
+    // 0296 centring still applies on this path.
+    if (!SDL_BlitSurface(_tf_src, &srcrect, _tf_dst, &dstrect))
+    {
+      LOG_ERROR("Renderer::drawTileFast: SDL_BlitSurface fallback failed: {}",
+                SDL_GetError());
+    }
+  }
 }
 
 // DOS-PORT (patch 0132, Phase 11 wave-35 mds_tilemap_bg drawTileFast
